{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not make for yourselves.</b> Even though you will be subjugated by the nations — like that one who sold himself to gentiles — do not exchange your glory for what does not profit. This is so that they not go astray, as they recalled, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 105a) that many went astray in the time of exile, saying to the prophets: 'A slave whose master sold him, and a woman whose husband divorced her — does the one have any claim upon the other?' For even after all subjugation, you are My servants, as they recalled of blessed memory (ibid.), for the prophets answered them thus: 'David My servant, Nebuchadnezzar My servant — a slave who acquired property, to whom does the property belong, to whom?'" "<b>For I am HaShem your Elohim.</b> Whom do they long for, even in the days of subjugation — as it says: וְאַף גַּם זֹאת לֹא מְאַסְתִּים (Leviticus 26:44) — for I am HaShem your Elohim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Sforno quotes a passage from Sanhedrin 105a; the phrase אשה שגרשה בעלה (whose husband divorced her) appears in the Talmudic discussion in context of the same sugya."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:09.690283904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}